# .env.example: a TEMPLATE for your settings. It is committed to git, so it must
# only ever contain placeholders, never a real key or password.
#
# 1. Copy it:   cp .env.example .env
# 2. Put real values in .env only (never in a chat, an issue, a commit or public/).
# 3. Restart `npm run dev` after every change to .env.
# 4. For the live site, add the same variables in Vercel → Settings → Environment
#    Variables, then redeploy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI feature (optional): any OpenAI-compatible provider. See TOOLS.md.
# Run `npm run models` to list the model IDs your key can use.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
LLM_API_KEY=paste-your-key-here
LLM_MODEL=paste-a-model-id-from-npm-run-models
# Example only, may be outdated: LLM_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest

# Groq:        LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# OpenRouter:  LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1   (use a model ID ending in :free)
# Ollama:      LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1       (your own computer only; LLM_API_KEY=ollama)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (week 7): Supabase. Leave these commented out until then.
# The publishable key is designed to be seen by browsers, but it is ONLY safe
# when row-level security (RLS) is enabled on every table, with policies that
# say who may read and write each row. You set that up in week 7.
# NEVER put the secret (service-role) key in this project's front end.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=paste-your-publishable-key-here
